%% Overview only. The focused diagrams next to this figure prove each invariant separately.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Staff as Staff<br/>POS
  participant BFF as BFF<br/>guards
  participant Order as Order<br/>order owner
  participant Catalog as Catalog<br/>stock owner
  participant Event as Outbox / Kafka / KDS

  Staff->>BFF: Confirm pending order
  BFF->>BFF: Verify JWT, tenant, permission
  BFF->>Order: Verified confirm command
  Order->>Order: Lock order and bill<br/>inside tenant scope

  alt Order already PROCESSING
    Order-->>BFF: Return current state
    BFF-->>Staff: Confirmation already applied
  else Order is PENDING and bill is OPEN
    Order->>Catalog: Deduct stock<br/>idempotency key + payload hash
    Catalog-->>Order: APPLIED or REPLAYED<br/>reservationVersion
    Order->>Order: Commit PROCESSING + items<br/>+ stockReservationVersion + outbox
    Order-->>BFF: Confirmation success
    BFF-->>Staff: Confirmation success
    Order-->>Event: Relay committed order.confirmed
    Event->>Event: Kitchen creates KDS ticket
  else Invalid order or bill state
    Order-->>BFF: Structured validation error
    BFF-->>Staff: Show confirmation error
  end

  Note over Order,Catalog: Order never writes Catalog DB directly.<br/>Focused figures below show commit boundary, retry, compensation and async side effect.
